{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479034-questions-about-relics","id":1479034,"title":"Questions about Relics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-17T15:04:19-07:00","id":1479034,"title":"Questions about Relics","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have many questions about Relics, and <b>especially about a Teros Scion,</b> please bear with me and help me to answer them:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>For a Relic that grants access to a Purview. </i>To use the Innate power the only thing needed is to be in contact with the relic, right?</li> <li><i>IF</i> the answer to the previous question is YES, can I just have my relics be subdermal, submuscular, or bone attached? Seems very fitting to the whole scientific paradigm the Teros have.</li> <li>Is there any flaw or additional point cost that represents a Relic that only works for its wielder? Biometric, spiritually or magically attuned.</li> <li><i>For a Relic that grants access to a Purview. </i>There is a Flaw that states that the Relic must be recharged every time after usage... Does this apply to the Innate Powers too?</li> </ol>The whole idea is to have a character that uses the relics as minimally intrusive cybernetic augmentations, this would limit the potential Motifs and usage, but for the character is just a way to access &quot;plug and play&quot; (innate) powers.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Clarity 04-21-2022, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T03:18:19-07:00","id":1479069,"title":"","content":"1) I rule it that way, yes.<br /> <br /> 2) Sure, but put the Concealable or Innocuous Tag on it (Origin, page 125) to represent the advantage of it being basically invisible to the naked eye.<br /> <br /> 3) On Scion: Hero page 211: \u201cRelic only functions if user inputs a password or speaks a particular phrase, takes an action; once confirmed, Relic functions for the scene\u201d. It\u2019s a one dot flaw and it basically has the effect you want. You just need to reword it.<br /> <br /> 4) That\u2019s how I rule it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T12:20:29-07:00","id":1479255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479034-questions-about-relics?p=1479069#post1479069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I rule it that way, yes.<br /> <br /> 2) Sure, but put the Concealable or Innocuous Tag on it (Origin, page 125) to represent the advantage of it being basically invisible to the naked eye.<br /> <br /> 3) On Scion: Hero page 211: \u201cRelic only functions if user inputs a password or speaks a particular phrase, takes an action; once confirmed, Relic functions for the scene\u201d. It\u2019s a one dot flaw and it basically has the effect you want. You just need to reword it.<br /> <br /> 4) That\u2019s how I rule it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, on option 3, I was looking for a permanent active relic, but physically bonded. To give the character a unique feeling and avoid having everyone requesting internal relics (while keeping the cybernetic flavour on this guy).<br /> <br /> I think the one dot flaw would be redundant with point 1. IF you need to touch it for it to work AND the flaw action is to have physical contact, the flaw is no flaw at all, and it would be power gaming.<br /> <br /> The flaw could be that it only works when connected to the nervous system (or inside the muscles, something like that) so the Relic is well protected but once lost or removed it is a pain to make it work again. Giving the character a real vulnerability (albeit one very well hidden). <b>D</b><b><b>oes</b> this option make sense to be covered by that one dot flaw?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Clarity 04-21-2022, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T13:08:53-07:00","id":1479260,"title":"","content":"What you are describing almost sounds like it would be the Natural Tag which would cost extra because it is basically part of the user's body.<br /> <br /> But if you want to keep it as a Flaw I would personally say it isn't severe enough to be more than 1 dot, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T13:50:08-07:00","id":1479264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479034-questions-about-relics?p=1479260#post1479260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you are describing almost sounds like it would be the <b>Natural Tag which would cost extra </b>because it is basically part of the user's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont have my books here, but how many points will this raise the cost of the Relic?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479034-questions-about-relics?p=1479260#post1479260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you want to keep it as a Flaw I would personally say it isn't severe enough to be more than 1 dot, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Restating the question, <b>will it make sense to have that one dot Flaw</b>: <i>\u201cRelic only functions if the user inputs a password or speaks a particular phrase, takes an action; once confirmed, Relic functions for the scene\u201d </i> <b>with the action being <i>touching a bone/inner organ/nerves</i>, to guarantee having a permanent active Relic</b> (every scene is in contact so it never stops working) WHILE still being limiting since removal would mean no easy way to replace it (requiring major surgery)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T06:53:19-07:00","id":1479334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479034-questions-about-relics?p=1479264#post1479264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont have my books here, but how many points will this raise the cost of the Relic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Natural is a one-point tag, so it adds one dot to the cost of the Relic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479034-questions-about-relics?p=1479264#post1479264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restating the question, <b>will it make sense to have that one dot Flaw</b>: <i>\u201cRelic only functions if the user inputs a password or speaks a particular phrase, takes an action; once confirmed, Relic functions for the scene\u201d </i> <b>with the action being <i>touching a bone/inner organ/nerves</i>, to guarantee having a permanent active Relic</b> (every scene is in contact so it never stops working) WHILE still being limiting since removal would mean no easy way to replace it (requiring major surgery)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the Relic is implanted is mostly a benefit, because it means it can never be disarmed or stolen. Aristarkos's idea of giving it the Natural tag makes a lot of sense, and that should come with the one-dot cost noted above. Apart from that benefit, the fact that the Relic only works for one person is not significant enough to warrant either a cost or a rebate, so the whole package balances out at a one-dot cost.<br /> <br /> If you want to take the suggestion of requiring a specific password to activate, that's a one-dot Flaw that balances out the cost of the implant. Otherwise, you can just leave it as a one-dot benefit and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","user":"gscrap","date":".  Clarification after re-reading the rest of the thread. 04-23-2022, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}